{
  "version": "v1.3",
  "naming_set": "chemist_style",
  "notes": "Mapping-only attachpoint convention:\n- Scaffold groups (kind=scaffold): the attach atom is the atom mapped as :1 in `smarts`.\n- Substituent groups (kind=substituent): the attach atom is the atom mapped as :2 in `smarts`.\n- If a group has multiple attachpoints, it may contain both :1 and :2 (or multiple mapped atoms) in `smarts`.\nThe legacy fields `attach_points` and `attach_labels` were removed; attachpoints are inferred from atom-maps in `smarts`.",
